# ==================================================================
# mausam-personalised — optional data-source keys
#
# Copy to `.env` for local dev (`.env` is git-ignored). For deploys,
# put the same names in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.
#
# REALITY CHECK (read before pasting keys):
# This is a zero-build static PWA on GitHub Pages. There is no server,
# so nothing here runs automatically. Two honest patterns exist:
#   (a) per-user browser key (what the app does today for IMD + Gemini:
#       Settings stores it in localStorage, calls go straight to the API);
#   (b) a tiny serverless proxy that holds the key server-side
#       (the only way a key is actually secret after deploy).
# Keys shipped inside the deployed bundle are PUBLIC, so only embed
# free/low-risk keys you are willing to rotate.
# ==================================================================

# ---- data.gov.in CPCB feed — ABANDONED (2026-10-31) -----------------
# The owner could never obtain a working key (registration is approval-
# gated) and api.data.gov.in is unreachable from datacenter IPs anyway.
# The CPCB station AQI this file once planned now arrives via OpenAQ
# (below) — its India rows ARE the CPCB/DPCC/UPPCB feed.
DATA_GOV_IN_API_KEY=
DATA_GOV_IN_CPCB_RESOURCE_ID=3b01bcb8-0b14-4abf-b6f2-c1bfd384ba69

# ---- OPENAQ v3 — LIVE ground-station AQI (shipped v0.8.40) ----------
# Free key: https://openaq.org → Sign up → API keys. Docs: https://docs.openaq.org
# CALL: GET https://api.openaq.org/v3/locations?coordinates=28.67,77.45&radius=25000
#       (auth via header: X-API-Key: <KEY>)
# NOTE: the demo key ships BAKED into src/api/keys.js (owner-approved,
# public by design, rotate in one place); a per-user Settings key wins.
OPENAQ_API_KEY=

# ---- NASA FIRMS — farm-fire hotspots (shipped v0.8.40, key baked) ---
# Free MAP_KEY (instant, no approval): https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# CALL: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area/csv/<MAP_KEY>/VIIRS_SNPP_NRT/77,28,79,29/2
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# ---- NO KEY NEEDED (shipped, zero-config) ---------------------------
# NASA POWER (MERRA-2 reanalysis) + Open-Meteo archive (ERA5) form the
# temperature's independent witness pair (src/api/witness.js, v0.8.41):
#   https://power.larc.nasa.gov/api/temporal/daily/point?parameters=T2M&community=AG&latitude=28.7&longitude=77.7&start=20261028&end=20261031&format=JSON
#   https://archive-api.open-meteo.com/v1/archive?latitude=28.7&longitude=77.7&daily=temperature_2m_mean
# indianapi.in Weather API: keys issued, but their endpoints return
# HTTP 500 for every city/id (broken upstream) — NOT integrated; when
# they fix it the key can be baked like the others.

# ---- IMD OFFICIAL — already wired into Settings (per-user browser key)
# Register free: https://api.imd.gov.in → Create Account → subscribe City Forecast
# Listed here only so local dev tooling can share the same key.
IMD_API_KEY=

# ---- GEMINI — Mitra's live LLM (per-user browser key today)
# Free: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ---- OPTIONAL / FUTURE ---------------------------------------------
# Copernicus CDS (heavy reanalysis; the app already uses Open-Meteo's
# archive API for "this week last year", so this is research-only)
CDSAPI_URL=https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/api
CDSAPI_KEY=

# Shared secret for a future key-signing proxy (Cloudflare Worker etc.)
PROXY_SHARED_SECRET=
